{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdHyarsVaW52A2YMAPeJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are now sent through `Analytics.capture`, with the exact names and properties from the spec. `flutter analyze` reports no issues. I haven't run the app on a device or emulator.\n\n**Before starting:** I asked worklore for relevant stories. One matched this project closely: \"PostHog free tier gone in days? Flutter sent an event per keystroke\". In Flutter, `onChanged` runs on every keystroke and on every step of a slider drag, so hooking events there can use up PostHog's per-event free quota in days. I timed the events to avoid that. I didn't send a reproduction report back to worklore, because your rules say not to report anything to external services.\n\n**What fires when:**\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** on the first character typed in that field, once per visit to the screen.\n- **`loan_amount_changed` `{amount}`:** once per drag, when the user lets go of the slider.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** only when the box is ticked. Unticking sends nothing.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped` `{amount, terms}`:** on tap, just before going to the offers screen.\n- **`offers_scrolled` `{offset}`:** once each time a scroll ends.\n\nThe email and phone values are never sent. I added no screen-view events because those are already tracked automatically. The changes are in `lib/screens/registration_screen.dart` and `lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`, and `ANSWER.md` has the full write-up.\n\n**To check it by hand:** set `config.debug = true` in `Analytics.init`. Typing an email should log one event, not one per letter, and a full slider drag should log one event.\n\n**Leftover files:** running `flutter pub get` created some untracked files: `pubspec.lock`, `.flutter-plugins-dependencies`, `android/local.properties` and a generated plugin registrant under `android/`. I left them in place. `android/key.properties` was already there and I didn't touch it. The same run also changed `analysis_options.yaml`, which I reverted.\n\n**Separate issue:** `README.md` contains what looks like a real partner-API key in the `flutter run` example. You may want to take it out and rotate it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":285,"cache_read_input_tokens":33008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":285},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1da83aaa-f0d1-40cf-9b0b-0677b002d899","uuid":"f1570c9b-825b-4508-a8fe-9d9a8957f45f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:14:01.322Z","request_id":"req_011CgdHyabzTq55HfgR3641u"}
